@startuml components
!theme plain
title swarma-dispatcher v0.3: callers, core, privileged operations (v0 command and v1 daemon share one core)

actor "Person\n(curator agent-user)" as P
node "Orchestrator agent\n(registered caller key)" as O
node "Board spawn path\n(later, via adapter)" as B
node "swarma-session-host\n(SH2+ service: metadata, fences)" as SH
rectangle "swarma-dispatcher\n(service account swarma-dispatcher)" as D {
  component "core\n(inputs, allocations agent/1, executions run/1,\neffect table, claims, journal, reconcile)" as CORE
  component "v0 command\n(sudo -u swarma-dispatcher, signed request)" as CMD
  component "v1 daemon\n(socket, queue, events)" as DMN
  component "supervisors\n(one per execution)" as SUP
  component "v0 internal service-only sweep timer\n(lifetimes, reconcile; v1 daemon internal)" as SW
}
component "Curator launch caller\n(compose plan)" as CUR
component "swarma-user-manager\n(user.create, user.retire, exec.stop)" as H
component "swarma-user-launcher\n(launch.start → start receipt)" as L
component "swarma-credential-broker\n(bind with caller dependency, lease)" as BR
node "curator-run narrow exec mode\n(agent account; first broker consumer)" as E
node "swarma-session-runner\n(SH2+ agent account: PTY/app-server, renewal)" as SR

P --> CUR : compose plan
CUR --> CMD : caller-composed plan; dispatch-op/1\nsigned domain: swarma-dispatcher request/1
O --> DMN : dispatch/1 + signature
B ..> DMN : adapter (later)
SH ..> DMN : launch request (no embedded broker client; later)
SH ..> SR : session metadata / input (later)
SR ..> BR : own broker connection (qualified later integration)
CMD --> CORE
DMN --> CORE
SW --> CORE
CORE --> H : no-argument sudo; closed request on stdin\ncreate / retire / stop (own generations only; distinct effect IDs)
CORE --> BR : bind / unbind (distinct effect IDs)\nlease chain + caller chain
CORE --> SUP
SUP --> L : no-argument sudo; launch.start on stdin\n{request_id: E-launch, generation, execution_id, epoch}
L --> E : receipt while root; clear groups; set GID/UID; exec\n(immutable plan FD3; own broker connection)
E --> BR : lease (own connection); broker re-checks\nthe caller dependency every time
note bottom of CORE
  Root (caller principal, request_id) is correlation;
  E-create, E-bind and E-launch are distinct receiver keys (§4.5).
  Capacity: v0 refuses; v1 queues. Quota/authority: always refuse.
end note
note right of E
  Caller composes; executor verifies and executes only.
  No profile resolution; no network except broker.
  Versioned intake/Decision 0021 amendment and
  credential qualification required before activation.
end note
@enduml
